         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/29461414-27c7-47f5-a022-2eb06a1ad173,1792451081418/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C0%2C1920%2C1080%29%3B' alt='Composite photo showing two headshots. On the left, a man in a suit, on the right a woman in a suit.' width='620' height='349' title='Incumbent Mayor of Pickering Kevin Ashe will be facing city councillor Lisa Robinson in the municipal election. Ashe has criticized Robinson&apos;s conduct and moved the city&apos;s council meetings online last year, citing safety concerns caused by her supporters.'/><p>With one week until election day, voters in Pickering, Whitby and Oshawa are preparing to choose their next mayor. Here’s a look at the candidates and the context shaping each race.</p>]]></description>
